-- title:
--   Igusa's degree bound over the residue field of A∩ k₀
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and $M\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M$, let $H\le(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and let $\Gamma_H(M)\le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ be [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), the image in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of the preimage of $H$ under the homomorphism $\Gamma_0(M)\to(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ sending a matrix to the class of its lower-right entry. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a nonunit of $A$, and let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ such that every $a\in A$ admits $c\in k_0\cap A$ with $a-c$ in the maximal ideal of $A$. Write $\kappa_0$ for the residue field of the valuation subring $A\cap k_0$ of $k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$), and let $F_0=$ [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) $\kappa_0\,\Gamma_H(M)$ be the subfield of $\kappa_0((q^{\mathbb{Z}}))$ generated over $\kappa_0$ by all quotients $\iota(p_f)/\iota(p_g)$ of the $\kappa_0$-reductions of integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g\in\mathbb{Z}[[q]]$ of modular forms $f,g$ of a common weight for $\Gamma_H(M)$, with $\iota(p_g)\neq 0$. Let $x\in F_0$ have underlying Laurent series $q^{-1}\cdot(E_4^3\eta^{-24})$ reduced to $\kappa_0$, i.e. [`ModularCurve.jqModC`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15) $\kappa_0$. Then the index of $\Gamma_H(M)\sqcup\langle -1\rangle$ in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ is at most the degree $[F_0:\kappa_0(x)]$, where $\kappa_0(x)$ is the intermediate field generated by $x$.
--
--   This is Igusa's lower bound for the degree of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_H(M)$ over the rational subfield generated by the reduced $j$-expansion, in residue characteristic $q$ prime to the level, here transported from the residue field of $A$ itself to the residue field of the smaller valuation ring $A\cap k_0$, the hypothesis on $k_0$ guaranteeing that the two residue fields agree. It feeds the identification of Gauss-type valuation subrings attached to full and to $\Gamma_H$-level modular function fields at primes not dividing the level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_index_gammaH_le_finrank_adjoin_jqModC_qExpFunctionFieldC_residueField_comap.lean

